# User-scoped chat (critical)

## Source of truth
Chat delivery MUST go through the API (`/api/chat/*`) so both participants see the same messages in the database (`conversations` / `messages`).

Local `localStorage` is only a legacy purge helper — never the delivery path.

## Never do this
- `localStorage.setItem('vibra_local_chats', ...)` or any **shared** key for conversations/messages
- Sending a message only on the sender device without `POST /api/chat/conversations/:id/messages`
- Opening a DM without `POST /api/chat/with/:peerUserId` (creates membership for both users)

## Always do this
- Open DM: `POST /api/chat/with/:peerUserId`
- List: `GET /api/chat/conversations`
- Messages: `GET /api/chat/conversations/:id/messages`
- Send: `POST /api/chat/conversations/:id/messages` with `{ content }`
- Reject self-chats (`peer.userId === currentUser.id`)
- Purge legacy key `vibra_local_chats` on auth/chat load

## Why
A shared browser chat key made a new model see someone else’s messages, and local-only send meant the model never received client messages. Server membership fixes both.
